---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Experience — Maxime de Visscher"
  description="Professional experience and long-term client collaborations by Maxime de Visscher, Creative Technologist and UX Architect."
>
  <SiteNav currentPath="/experience/" />
  <main id="main" class="subpage-main">
    <section class="page-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Professional background</p>
      <h1 id="experience-title">Experience</h1>
      <p>
        Long-term collaborations where UX, technology and product decisions have to work together.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap mission-list" aria-label="Selected experience">
      <article class="mission">
        <div class="mission-heading">
          <h2>Mbrella</h2>
          <p class="metadata">Freelance UX Architect<br />June 2021 to present</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mission-content">
          <p>
            I joined Mbrella while it was still a startup and have contributed as it grew into a
            scale-up. I <strong>shape the UX</strong> of its mobility-budget platform for HR teams and{' '}
            <strong>build mobile</strong> and <strong>AI tools</strong>. The work extends beyond wireframes to
            senior front-end development and building the mobile application in React Native.
          </p>
          <p>
            One example started in the first hours after OpenAI introduced GPT-4o: could it handle
            mobility documents better than a traditional OCR pipeline? I took the idea from{' '}
            <strong>hypothesis to integration</strong>, working on the technical architecture, prototype and
            scanner experience, testing whether it <strong>solved the problem better</strong>. I
            created anonymized datasets, test tools and benchmarks to compare extraction quality,
            response time and cost.
          </p>
          <p>
            I also <strong>connected our teams to the complete API</strong> by building Mbrella's
            first internal MCP server, giving development and support teams access{' '}
            <strong>directly from Claude</strong>.
          </p>
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://www.mbrella.eu/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Visit Mbrella <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="mission">
        <div class="mission-heading">
          <h2>Emakina</h2>
          <p class="metadata">
            Technical Presales &amp; New Business<br />Strategist &amp; IT Consultant<br />2006 to
            2019
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mission-content">
          <p>
            For thirteen years, I worked with Emakina across technical presales, new business
            pitches, UX and R&amp;D. I helped <strong>New Business teams</strong> turn{' '}
            <strong>fuzzy briefs</strong> into <strong>workable approaches</strong>, bringing technical
            expertise to balance the client's budget, functional needs and delivery constraints,
            with <strong>users at the centre</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            During pitches, I brought user-centred ideas into the conversation early and made
            them tangible through user flows, information architecture, wireframes and interface
            concepts. Moving between strategy and UX work, I connected <strong>business ambitions</strong>{' '}
            with <strong>the people using the product</strong> and <strong>the teams building it</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            I had the opportunity to contribute to projects for clients including Audi, the European
            Parliament, Musée d’Orsay, Proximus, RTBF Auvio and Thalys.
          </p>
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://www.empathylab.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Now Empathy Lab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
